md`# brain-git

Git repositories for a Cloud Brain, kept by [Cloudflare Artifacts](https://developers.cloudflare.com/artifacts/). The service makes a repository and hands out a token for it. Cloning, fetching and pushing are plain \`git\` over HTTPS against Cloudflare's own address, with that token; no git traffic passes this Brain. Each answer is Cloudflare's, its errors included.

| Method | Cloudflare endpoint |
|---|---|
| \`git.create?name=\` | \`POST /accounts/ACCOUNT/artifacts/namespaces/BASE/repos\` with \`{ name, default_branch: "main" }\`. The answer has \`remote\` and a first write token. |
| \`git.get?name=\` | \`GET …/repos/NAME\`: the repository, with its \`remote\`. |
| \`git.list?limit=&cursor=\` | \`GET …/repos\`. |
| \`git.token?name=&scope=&seconds=\` | \`POST …/tokens\` with \`{ repo, scope, ttl }\`. \`scope\` is \`read\` (when not given) or \`write\`. \`seconds\` is ${gitDefaults.seconds} when not given, from ${gitDefaults.least} to ${gitDefaults.most}. The answer's \`plaintext\` is the token. |
| \`git.delete?name=\` | \`DELETE …/repos/NAME\`. |

All but \`get\` and \`list\` are sent with POST. The parameters are in the query string so a rule can read them (\`request.params.name\`, \`request.params.scope\`); none is a secret. A token is in the body of the answer and nowhere else.

\`\`\`sh
# TOKEN is plaintext from git.token, REMOTE is remote from git.get
git -c http.extraHeader="Authorization: Bearer $TOKEN" clone "$REMOTE" work
\`\`\`

## Whose repository

Every repository of this Brain is in one Artifacts namespace, named for the Brain (\`cb4\`). The service adds the namespace; no parameter changes it, so a caller cannot reach a repository of another Brain on the same Cloudflare account.

Inside the namespace a name belongs to whoever made it (\`gitTenant\`, \`gitRepo\`):

| Caller | Their repository \`notes\` is | Reaches |
|---|---|---|
| the owner, a token, a Worker of the Brain | \`notes\` | every repository of the Brain, a member's by its full name |
| an account the owner gave the method (\`did:…\`), and that account's Workers | \`m-ID-notes\`, where ID is 10 hex of the SHA-256 of the DID | names that start with \`m-ID-\` and no other |

A member gives the short name or the full one. A name on Cloudflare is at most 40 characters, so a member's short name is at most 27. \`git.list\` answers a member only their own: it is one page of Cloudflare's list with the others taken out, so a page can be short or empty while \`cursor\` says there is more, and any count beside it is the Brain's. The owner cannot make a repository whose name starts like a member's.

## Who can call

The owner, a token that names the method and an account the owner gave it (\`grant.put\`). To hold a token to reading one repository: \`caller.session || (request.params.name == "core" && request.params.scope != "write")\` as the rule of \`com.lopecode.brain.git.token\`.

## The Cloudflare token

The service declares \`cloudflare: ["${gitDefaults.group}"]\`. The deployer mints a Cloudflare API token with that one permission and binds it to this Worker alone. That token can make, read and delete every Artifacts repository of the Cloudflare account, in any namespace, which is why the namespace is not a parameter.

## The price

\`create\` and \`token\` cost $${gitDefaults.usd} a call. Cloudflare charges $0.15 for 1,000 operations after the first 10,000 a month, and an operation is a create, a clone, a pull or a push. The git traffic a token leads to is not seen by this Brain, so the price of the token stands for it. The number is a guess: 6 operations.

## Limits, Cloudflare's

1 GB a repository, 32 MB a file, 2,000 git requests in 10 s a repository (read 2026-10-10). Workers Paid only.

Not built: \`fork\`, \`import\`, revoking one token, giving another account a repository of yours.`
// %%
gitDefaults = ({ seconds: 3600, least: 60, most: 86400, usd: 0.001, group: "Artifacts Write" })
// %%
// The start of a caller's repository names. "" is the Brain's own: the owner, a token, the deployer, a Worker of the
// Brain. A person is m-ID-, as a member's Worker is brain-m-ID-NAME. null: no repositories.
gitTenant = async (who) =>
  who === "owner" || who === "deployer" || /^token:/.test(who || "") || /^worker:brain(-(?!m-)|$)/.test(who || "") ? "" : /^did:/.test(who || "") ? "m-" + (await sha256(who)).slice(0, 10) + "-" : null
// %%
// How a member's repository starts on Cloudflare. The 10 is the length of a member's id (memberId in brain-deployer).
gitMember = /^m-[0-9a-f]{10}-/
// %%
// The name on Cloudflare of the repository a caller means, or null when the name is not theirs to use. The name
// Cloudflare holds is at most 40 characters, so one this service made is one it takes back.
gitRepo = (prefix, name) => {
  const ok = (n) => /^[a-z0-9][a-z0-9._-]{0,39}$/.test(n);
  if (typeof name !== "string" || !ok(name)) return null;
  if (prefix === "") return name;
  const full = name.startsWith(prefix) ? name : gitMember.test(name) ? "" : prefix + name;
  return full.length > prefix.length && ok(full) ? full : null;
}
// %%
git_service = cloudflare.Service(
  "git",
  async (request) => {
    const refuse = (status, error, message) => new Response(JSON.stringify({ error, message }), { status, headers: { "content-type": "application/json" } });
    const url = new URL(request.url), what = url.pathname.split(".").pop(), q = url.searchParams;
    const verb = { create: "POST", token: "POST", delete: "POST", get: "GET", list: "GET" }[what];
    if (!verb) return refuse(404, "MethodNotImplemented", "git.create, git.get, git.list, git.token and git.delete");
    if (request.method !== verb) return refuse(405, "InvalidRequest", "git." + what + " is sent with " + verb);
    const prefix = await gitTenant(request.headers.get("x-brain-caller"));
    if (prefix === null) return refuse(403, "Forbidden", "this caller has no repositories");
    const space = "/artifacts/namespaces/" + config.base;
    const pass = (r) => new Response(r.body, { status: r.status, headers: { "content-type": r.headers.get("content-type") || "application/json" } });
    const send = (path, method, body) => cloudflareApi.fetch(space + path, { method, ...(body ? { headers: { "content-type": "application/json" }, body: JSON.stringify(body) } : {}) });
    if (what === "list") {
      const r = await send("/repos?" + new URLSearchParams([...q].filter(([k]) => k === "limit" || k === "cursor")), "GET");
      if (prefix === "" || !r.ok) return pass(r);
      const data = await r.json();
      return new Response(JSON.stringify({ ...data, result: (Array.isArray(data.result) ? data.result : []).filter((x) => String(x && x.name).startsWith(prefix)) }), { headers: { "content-type": "application/json" } });
    }
    const repo = gitRepo(prefix, q.get("name"));
    if (!repo) return refuse(400, "InvalidRequest", "name is a repository of yours: a lower-case letter or digit, then up to 39 of a-z 0-9 . _ - (26 for an account that is not the owner)");
    if (what === "create") {
      if (prefix === "" && gitMember.test(repo)) return refuse(400, "InvalidRequest", "a name that starts m-ID- is a member's to make");
      return pass(await send("/repos", "POST", { name: repo, default_branch: "main" }));
    }
    if (what === "get") return pass(await send("/repos/" + repo, "GET"));
    if (what === "delete") return pass(await send("/repos/" + repo, "DELETE"));
    const scope = q.get("scope") || "read", seconds = q.get("seconds") === null ? gitDefaults.seconds : Number(q.get("seconds"));
    if (scope !== "read" && scope !== "write") return refuse(400, "InvalidRequest", "scope is read or write");
    if (!Number.isInteger(seconds) || seconds < gitDefaults.least || seconds > gitDefaults.most) return refuse(400, "InvalidRequest", "seconds is a whole number from " + gitDefaults.least + " to " + gitDefaults.most);
    return pass(await send("/tokens", "POST", { repo, scope, ttl: seconds }));
  },
  {
    cloudflare: [gitDefaults.group],
    methods: {
      "com.lopecode.brain.git.create": { type: "procedure", who: "owner", price: String(gitDefaults.usd) },
      "com.lopecode.brain.git.get": { type: "query", who: "owner" },
      "com.lopecode.brain.git.list": { type: "query", who: "owner" },
      "com.lopecode.brain.git.token": { type: "procedure", who: "owner", price: String(gitDefaults.usd) },
      "com.lopecode.brain.git.delete": { type: "procedure", who: "owner" }
    }
  }
)
// %%
git_announce = {
  plugins.add("workers", git_service, { invalidation });
  return "announced git_service";
}
// %%
md`## Tests`
// %%
gitRig = async () => {
  const seen = [];
  const repos = [{ name: "core" }, { name: "m-" + (await sha256("did:plc:alice")).slice(0, 10) + "-notes" }, { name: "m-0000000000-other" }];
  const sim = await simulate(git_service, {
    secrets: { CF_TOKEN: "minted-1", BRAIN_KEY: "k" },
    config: { base: "cb4", account: "acct" },
    fetch: async (request) => {
      const body = request.method === "GET" || request.method === "DELETE" ? null : await request.json();
      seen.push({ verb: request.method, url: request.url.replace("https://api.cloudflare.com/client/v4/accounts/acct/artifacts/namespaces/", ""), authorization: request.headers.get("authorization"), body });
      const path = new URL(request.url).pathname;
      if (path.endsWith("/missing")) return new Response('{"success":false,"errors":[{"code":1000,"message":"not found"}]}', { status: 404, headers: { "content-type": "application/json" } });
      const result = path.endsWith("/tokens") ? { plaintext: "art_v1_secret?expires=9", expiresAt: 9 } : path.endsWith("/repos") && request.method === "GET" ? repos : { name: (body && body.name) || path.split("/").pop(), remote: "https://acct.artifacts.cloudflare.net/git/cb4/x.git" };
      return new Response(JSON.stringify({ success: true, result }), { headers: { "content-type": "application/json" } });
    }
  });
  const call = async (who, name, query = "", verb = name === "get" || name === "list" ? "GET" : "POST") => {
    const r = await sim.fetch("https://git.internal/xrpc/com.lopecode.brain.git." + name + (query ? "?" + query : ""), { method: verb, headers: { "x-brain-caller": who }, ...(verb === "POST" ? { body: "{}" } : {}) });
    return { status: r.status, data: await r.json() };
  };
  return { sim, seen, call, alice: "m-" + (await sha256("did:plc:alice")).slice(0, 10) + "-" };
}
// %%
test_each_method_is_one_call_to_artifacts_in_this_brains_namespace = {
  const rig = await gitRig();
  expect((await rig.call("owner", "create", "name=core")).data.result.remote).toMatch(/artifacts\.cloudflare\.net/);
  expect((await rig.call("owner", "get", "name=core")).status).toBe(200);
  expect((await rig.call("owner", "list", "limit=5&cursor=c&namespace=other")).data.result.length).toBe(3);
  expect((await rig.call("token:ci", "token", "name=core")).data.result.plaintext).toBe("art_v1_secret?expires=9");
  await rig.call("worker:brain-x-snapshot", "token", "name=core&scope=write&seconds=60");
  expect((await rig.call("owner", "delete", "name=core")).status).toBe(200);
  expect(rig.seen).toEqual([
    { verb: "POST", url: "cb4/repos", authorization: "Bearer minted-1", body: { name: "core", default_branch: "main" } },
    { verb: "GET", url: "cb4/repos/core", authorization: "Bearer minted-1", body: null },
    { verb: "GET", url: "cb4/repos?limit=5&cursor=c", authorization: "Bearer minted-1", body: null },
    { verb: "POST", url: "cb4/tokens", authorization: "Bearer minted-1", body: { repo: "core", scope: "read", ttl: 3600 } },
    { verb: "POST", url: "cb4/tokens", authorization: "Bearer minted-1", body: { repo: "core", scope: "write", ttl: 60 } },
    { verb: "DELETE", url: "cb4/repos/core", authorization: "Bearer minted-1", body: null }
  ]);
  // Cloudflare's refusal is the answer.
  expect(await rig.call("owner", "get", "name=missing")).toEqual({ status: 404, data: { success: false, errors: [{ code: 1000, message: "not found" }] } });
  return "6 calls";
}
// %%
test_a_member_reaches_their_own_repositories_and_no_other = {
  const rig = await gitRig(), alice = "did:plc:alice";
  // The short name and the full one are the same repository.
  await rig.call(alice, "create", "name=notes");
  await rig.call(alice, "token", "name=" + rig.alice + "notes&scope=write");
  expect(rig.seen.map((s) => s.body.name || s.body.repo)).toEqual([rig.alice + "notes", rig.alice + "notes"]);
  // The owner's core, as a member names it, is a repository of the member's own.
  await rig.call(alice, "token", "name=core");
  expect(rig.seen[2].body.repo).toBe(rig.alice + "core");
  // Another member's name, and a bare prefix, are refused before Cloudflare is asked.
  for (const name of ["m-0000000000-other", rig.alice, "", "Core", "a/b", "../core", "a".repeat(41)])
    for (const method of ["create", "token", "delete"]) expect((await rig.call(alice, method, "name=" + encodeURIComponent(name))).status).toBe(400);
  expect((await rig.call(alice, "get", "name=m-0000000000-other")).status).toBe(400);
  expect(rig.seen.length).toBe(3);
  // A member's longest name is 27, and the owner reaches it by the name Cloudflare holds.
  expect((await rig.call(alice, "create", "name=" + "a".repeat(28))).status).toBe(400);
  expect((await rig.call(alice, "create", "name=" + "a".repeat(27))).status).toBe(200);
  expect((await rig.call("owner", "delete", "name=" + rig.alice + "a".repeat(27))).status).toBe(200);
  expect((await rig.call(alice, "get", "name=" + rig.alice + "a".repeat(27))).status).toBe(200);
  expect(rig.seen.splice(3).map((s) => s.url)).toEqual(["cb4/repos", "cb4/repos/" + rig.alice + "a".repeat(27), "cb4/repos/" + rig.alice + "a".repeat(27)]);
  // A list is the member's own.
  expect((await rig.call(alice, "list")).data.result).toEqual([{ name: rig.alice + "notes" }]);
  // The owner reaches a member's repository by its full name, and does not make one.
  expect((await rig.call("owner", "token", "name=" + rig.alice + "notes")).status).toBe(200);
  expect((await rig.call("owner", "create", "name=" + rig.alice + "x")).status).toBe(400);
  // A caller that is nobody has none.
  for (const who of ["anonymous", "worker:brain-m-0000000000-x", "worker:other", ""]) expect((await rig.call(who, "list")).status).toBe(403);
  expect(await gitTenant("worker:brain")).toBe("");
  return "1 member, 4 nobodies";
}
// %%
test_git_refuses_a_bad_scope_a_bad_time_and_a_wrong_verb = {
  const rig = await gitRig();
  for (const query of ["scope=admin", "seconds=59", "seconds=86401", "seconds=1.5", "seconds=abc", "seconds="]) expect((await rig.call("owner", "token", "name=core&" + query)).status).toBe(400);
  expect((await rig.call("owner", "token", "name=core", "GET")).status).toBe(405);
  expect((await rig.call("owner", "delete", "name=core", "GET")).status).toBe(405);
  for (const other of ["fork", "import", "token/../../repos"]) expect((await rig.call("owner", other, "name=core")).status).toBe(404);
  expect(rig.seen.length).toBe(0);
  return "9 refused";
}
// %%
test_git_declares_one_cloudflare_permission_and_keeps_nothing = {
  const { meta, parts } = await git_service.emit();
  expect(meta.worker).toBe("brain-x-git");
  expect(meta.cloudflare).toEqual(["Artifacts Write"]);
  expect([meta.resources, meta.secrets, meta.calls]).toEqual([[], [], []]);
  expect(parts[0].text).toContain("__rt.platform.secrets.CF_TOKEN");
  // The owner's rule for a token that reads one repository.
  const rule = { allow: 'caller.session || (request.params.name == "core" && request.params.scope != "write")' };
  const ask = (params) => decide(rule, { caller: callerOf({ caller: "owner", via: "delegation:d1" }), origin: callerOf({ caller: "owner" }), request: { params } }).allow;
  expect([ask({ name: "core", scope: "read" }), ask({ name: "core", scope: "write" }), ask({ name: "other", scope: "read" })]).toEqual([true, false, false]);
  return meta.cloudflare[0];
}
// %%
import {cloudflare, cloudflareApi, config, simulate, decide, callerOf, sha256} from "@tomlarkworthy/cloudflare-iac"
// %%
import {plugins} from "@tomlarkworthy/plugin-registry"
// %%
import {expect} from "@tomlarkworthy/jest-expect-standalone"
